2ND ASCENSION GAME SUMMARY ("The Wizard Makes a Big Splash")

Dunamos the Wizard        St:18 Dx:18 Co:16 In:24 Wi:24 Ch:18  Chaotic
Astral Plane $:0  HP:290(400) Pw:103(515) AC:-41 Xp:29/90070586 T:61722

It's interesting to ascend for the second time and be able to make
comparisons. I realize how many spellbooks and tools I got last
time around, and how much harder some things are without them. The
two conveniences I missed most was that I never found a magic lamp,
nor a magic whistle. Taming is one of my favorite parts of the game;
walking through the dark clearing the level and *then* having to
round up a pair of pets and yank their leashes toward the staircase
tries one's patience.

I did find +oMagicMapping this time, which takes a lot of the tedium
out of Gehennom. However, as Janis recently posted, I ended up at
the Vibrating Square a lot less capable; the shortcut to the bottom
comes at a cost. Next time I'll at least use +oDetTreasure or !oObjDet.

This time HP was not a problem, and after SDSM and [oBrilliance I
ended up using all my wishes for magic markers. It is amazing how
complete your wizard's asc. kit can be in that scenario. I am
considering wishless/polyless for my next game; it would be fun to
try taking only what objects you find or are given.

The big "first" event for this game was displacing my pet giant
into the water and angering Anhur. It's one of those "put two and
two together" things that had never occurred to me; last game I
learned not to displace my pet when *he's* in the water; this game
I learned the reverse also has bad consequences. :-)

I lucked out on astral once again by finding Anhur's altar on the
first try. Getting in and back out of two altar rooms to get to the
third looks... really hard.

